    "1": {
      "note": "Making plans uses <strong>joek3</strong> (約) as its core verb — it covers everything from arranging a meet-up to making a date. To accept, <em>hou2</em> (好). To decline politely, the cultural move is <em>goi2 jat6 laa1</em> ('another day') rather than a flat no. The compound <em>dak1 haan4</em> (得閒, free/available) is paired with most invitation questions: <em>nei5 gei2 si4 dak1 haan4?</em> = 'when are you free?'",
